WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.450
Last term, our classroom fan ran all

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.590
weekend, with nobody in the room.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.160
Someone forgot to switch it off.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.040
A small sensor with one good

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.600
rule would never forget.

6
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.810
Today, you'll write that rule.

7
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.110
Today: IF this, THEN that, the rules

8
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.370
that let a device decide on its own.

9
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.620
A device that acts on its own

10
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.280
follows rules, each with two parts.

11
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.150
The IF part is a condition a sensor can

12
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.070
check: the room is above thirty degrees.

13
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.670
The THEN part is an action:

14
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.290
switch the fan on.

15
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.320
You live with rules like these.

16
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.710
IF the water tank is low,

17
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.530
THEN the pump starts.

18
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.780
IF it gets dark, THEN the

19
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.900
street light comes on.

20
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.440
One condition is often not enough.

21
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.040
IF the garden soil is dry AND it's

22
00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.820
early morning, THEN water it.

23
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.910
With AND, both must be true, so at

24
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.310
midday the pump waits, and less

25
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.530
water dries up in the sun.

26
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.470
OR works the other way:

27
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.410
either condition is enough.

28
00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.130
IF the smoke sensor detects smoke

29
00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.170
OR someone presses the fire

30
00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.370
button, THEN the alarm rings.

31
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.260
Quick check!

32
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.430
The school gate light should come on

33
00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.370
only for people arriving after dark.

34
00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.270
Which rule does that?

35
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:30.930
AND.

36
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.460
It must be dark, and

37
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.000
someone must be there.

38
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.540
With OR, the light would burn all

39
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.880
night, and flash on at noon

40
00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.740
whenever someone walked past.

41
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.030
A rule that looks right on paper can still

42
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.910
go wrong, so test it through a whole day.

43
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.310
At seven, the room is cool and empty.

44
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.620
After lunch, it's hottest.

45
00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.320
At five, everyone has gone

46
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.140
home, but it's still warm.

47
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.200
Now look for trouble.

48
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.350
The rule says: IF above thirty

49
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.530
degrees, THEN fan on.

50
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:12.390
At five, it's still thirty-one degrees, so

51
00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.910
the fan runs all evening for nobody.

52
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.380
Add AND a class is in, and it

53
00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.860
stops when everyone leaves.

54
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:21.920
Your turn.

55
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.780
A rule says: IF above thirty

56
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.900
degrees, THEN open the window.

57
00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:30.310
In your test, a storm comes at two,

58
00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.850
and rain pours onto the desks.

59
00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.690
What's the best fix?

60
00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.640
Add AND it isn't raining, so the window

61
00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.760
opens only when it's hot and dry.

62
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.730
Remember: IF a condition, THEN an action.

63
00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.050
AND needs both; OR needs either one.

64
00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.820
And test every rule through a day.

65
00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.910
Try it this week, at school or at home:

66
00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.010
write three rules for things around you,

67
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:02.250
like a fan, a light or a water tank.

68
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.660
Play each one through a day

69
00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.180
on paper, hour by hour.

70
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.790
Find one that goes wrong, and

71
00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.770
fix it with AND or OR.

72
00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.390
Next time: when should it switch?
